  "result": "Perfect! I found the document. The file `docs/requirements/issues.md` contains **REQ-061** which explicitly states the rule about issue numbering and scoping.\n\nThe requirement clearly shows that issue numbers are \"allocated per project and never reused\" (line 87). The key passage explains:\n\n> `nextIssueNumber(orgId, projectId)` returns a monotonically increasing integer **scoped to the project**; ... Numbers are never recycled ... because `ENG-142` having meant two different things at different points in the project's history would break every saved link, comment permalink and search result referencing it.\n\nThis explains why two different projects in the same workspace can each legitimately have issue #7—because the numbering scope is per-project, not per-workspace. The requirement explicitly states that \"a number is never handed out twice within its own scope,\" and the scope is the individual project.\n\nANSWER: docs/requirements/issues.md",
